# Generated by packages/tokens/build.mjs — build output, not authored source.
#
# stylelint-config-standard enforces AUTHORING style: modern color-function
# notation, percentage alpha, no duplicate selectors. None of that is meaningful
# for a file nobody types. Two concrete examples of why linting it is wrong
# rather than merely noisy:
#
#   * The rgba() values come from the design system's own token source. Rewriting
#     them to `rgb(0 0 0 / 24%)` to satisfy a style rule would mean the generated
#     CSS no longer matches the value a designer wrote, for no visual difference.
#   * `no-duplicate-selectors` fires on the two `body[data-jp-theme-name^=...]`
#     blocks, which are deliberately separate: one is Tier 2 (semantic, light),
#     one is Tier 3 (component). Merging them to satisfy the rule would destroy
#     the tier boundary the whole architecture rests on.
#
# The guard for these files is the CI freshness check — rebuild the tokens and
# assert a clean tree — not a style rule. Same reasoning as .prettierignore.
